Title 17 §§ 2851-2859 authorizes the municipal officers to determine that a building or structure is "dangerous" and to order appropriate corrective action either by the owner or by the town in the event that the owner does nothing. Other than in the case of a building that is so dangerous that immediate court action is required, there is no express authority given to the code enforcement officer to act under this statute. However, the

